extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 3: England printed 55-57 (cache p056-p058, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the cache and checked against renders of printed 56 and 57, where the stat block, skills and three of the five trait tables sit. The entry starts at the Dabuggh R.C.C. heading on printed 55 and ends at Secondary Skills on printed 57. || CATEGORY: an optional player race printed as an R.C.C. with its own skills, related and secondary, stored as printed; no occ_group, and a race. It agrees with its creature row (dabuggh, row 7) on every racial figure. || XP: the column headed Dubugghs, Earth & Star Child (so spelled) on the Experience Tables, printed 152 (cache p153), read off a render; the stat block names the same table. Every low bound is the previous high plus one. || POOLS: M.D.C. 2D4x10 plus 1D6 per level; P.P.E. 6D6+6; no hit points, a mega-damage creature. Horror Factor 10 applies only once it is recognized. || TRAITS: the five trait tables (features and appendages, mouth, eye, antenna, exoskeleton) are five pick-one groups of band-named options; the How Many table (one to five) is prose, so the cap is one per table and five in all, and the rolled number is the player''s to honour. Insect Strength''s 1D4+4 P.S., two arms'' two attacks, 360 degree sight''s +1 parry and dodge, and the exoskeleton M.D.C. are stored as bonuses on the option; the rest is prose. || METAMORPHOSIS: second_form carries the giant form''s +6 P.S. and +20 Spd; its 100 M.D.C. stays prose because a second form takes S.D.C. and hit points only, and the 3D6 M.D. bite is prose. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Math: Basic is Mathematics: Basic; Identify Plants & Fruits is Identify Plants & Fruit; Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals; Climb is Climbing. Faerie Speak has no language row and rides Language: Other at 70%, as England''s other classes carry a named tongue; two languages of choice at +20% are a two-pick Language: Other group. Hand to Hand: Expert is granted and Assassin can be selected if evil, no price printed: costs { assassin: 0 }. Pilot any is read to include the Horsemanship category at +5%. Pilot except spacecraft and robots drops Robots & Power Armor, Robot Combat and Space: rows. Science math only is the two Mathematics rows; Technical language, literacy, lore, computer operation and writing only is Computer Operation, Creative Writing and every Language:, Literacy and Lore: row. The natural track by smell 60% and swim 70% stay prose. || EQUIPMENT: back-pack, utility belt, pouches or sacks as one pouch, lighter, flashlight, knife. Not stored: energy pistol and energy rifle (none named), and either 1D6 grenades or a vibro-blade (a choice whose two halves have different quantities, which a pick cannot hold). Most use any human weapons, tools and vehicles but cannot build them."
