# Dabuggh

## Lore

Human-looking D-Bees with one or more insect or arachnid features: insect wings, compound eyes, the ability to spin a web. Natural enemies of the mantaz sectles, probably from the same world, the two races loathe each other. Dabugghs feed on the blood and organs of mammals, humans and D-Bees included, and are aggressive, predatory, territorial and driven to conquer and enslave. They are fearless warriors who respect strength, cunning and winning, energetic and inventive, and community or swarm oriented. Most hide their nature from other humanoids, whom they see as enemies or food.

## GM Notes

Few in the British Isles know how many dabugghs live there: most large kingdoms and towns, New Camelot included, have 2D6 of the most human-looking among them, at least six villages of 1D4x100 are wholly dabuggh, and a community of 1200 plus 500 D-Bees lives on a northern island. They outnumber the sectles two to one. They emerged from a rift decades ago and have colonies in Europe. A female lays 2D4 eggs each spring, hidden under leaves, sticks or bones, and their numbers are growing fast. Average NPC level 1D4+4. They love magic items and weapons.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dabuggh');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dabuggh';

